# Tier 3: every input that decides what the checks run or how strict they are. One gitignore-style path pattern per
# line, or "key <file pattern> <regex>": a changed line of that file that the regex matches.
#   .gate/bin/tier reads this file from main's checkout, so a pull request cannot take itself out of it.
#   .gate/bin/verify-trusted lays main's copy of every protected path over the candidate before main's checks run.
#   .gate/bin/verify (policy) requires .github/CODEOWNERS to end with exactly these paths, each with an owner, so GitHub
#   asks for the Human's review on them. A key line cannot be put in CODEOWNERS: tier alone guards it, and
#   verify-trusted keeps the candidate's manifest, since main's copy would undo its dependencies.
# A directory is written without a trailing "/": then the path itself is protected too, as a file, a directory or a link,
# in tier and in CODEOWNERS alike. .gate/bin/verify (policy) refuses a line that ends in "/".
# A repository adds what decides its own checks: a Makefile its gate_tests calls, a conftest.py that skips tests.
